          "citation": "145 Haw. 477 (2019)",
          "court": "Supreme Court of Hawai'i",
          "year": 2019,
          "date_decided": "2019-12-13",
          "holding": "The court held that termination under HRS § 587A-33 requires a finding that the proposed permanent plan is in the child's best interests, and that the ICA erred by substituting the more general family court provision, HRS § 571-61(b)(1)(E), to avoid that requirement.",
          "relevance": "The safe-family-home analysis is expressly tied to whether the parent can parent safely even with the assistance of a service plan.",
          "quote": "the family court erred in terminating Father’s parental rights under HRS § 587A-33, the CPA Provision, without finding that DHS’s proposed permanent plan was in KK’s best interests",
